    {
      "id": "7qgi7sm",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Key Basel III Requirements in India"
    },
    {
      "id": "w1ad9na",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "Minimum CRAR: 9% (vs 8% globally)",
        "Tier 1 Capital: 7% (Common Equity Tier 1 of 5.5%)",
        "Capital Conservation Buffer: 2.5%",
        "LCR (Liquidity Coverage Ratio): Banks must hold sufficient high-quality liquid assets",
        "NSFR (Net Stable Funding Ratio): Ensures long-term stable funding"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "pullQuote",
      "content": "RBI Regulations and Banking Norms serve as the structural framework for maintaining financial stability, credit discipline, and inclusive economic growth in India.",
      "id": "inoppjw"
    },
