    {
      "id": "cqrspib",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "4.4 SARFAESI Act, 2002"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "mqtl8k8",
      "content": "The Securitisation and Reconstruction of Financial Assets and Enforcement of Securities Interest (SARFAESI) Act allows banks and financial institutions to auction residential or commercial properties to recover loans without court intervention."
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "PSL targets differ by bank type: Domestic Commercial Banks require 40%, while Regional Rural Banks (RRBs) and Small Finance Banks (SFBs) require 75%.",
        "NPAs are categorized into three types: Substandard (<= 12 months), Doubtful (> 12 months), and Loss Assets (identified as uncollectible).",
        "SARFAESI Act provisions cannot be invoked for agricultural land or debt amounts below Rs. 1 lakh."
      ],
      "id": "2exoofg"
    },
    {
      "id": "at4scm7",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "Applicable for secured debts of Rs.1 lakh and above",
        "Bank issues demand notice; borrower has 60 days to pay",
        "If unpaid, bank can take possession of assets",
        "ARCs (Asset Reconstruction Companies) can purchase NPAs from banks"
      ]
    },
